1
00:00:00,430 --> 00:00:01,430
(All characters and organisations in this drama are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,430 --> 00:00:02,430
(Filming with minors followed broadcast guidelines,)

3
00:00:02,430 --> 00:00:03,500
(and generative AI was used in select scenes.)

4
00:00:10,040 --> 00:00:12,810
I won't disappoint Seo Hyun anymore,

5
00:00:13,340 --> 00:00:14,570
or hurt her,

6
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:16,580
or confuse her.

7
00:00:19,150 --> 00:00:21,150
What do you mean by that?

8
00:00:21,550 --> 00:00:23,620
It means I'm done with us just being friends.

9
00:00:24,920 --> 00:00:25,990
Mu Jin!

10
00:00:28,060 --> 00:00:31,990
So, you're telling me...

11
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:35,700
Not like a brother and sister, but as a man and a woman.

12
00:00:36,830 --> 00:00:38,200
Let's date for real, Seo Hyun.

13
00:00:39,170 --> 00:00:40,570
What do you think you're doing?

14
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:42,700
Are you toying with my Seo Hyun, or what?

15
00:00:42,770 --> 00:00:45,240
- Is my daughter a pushover? - Mom!

16
00:00:46,010 --> 00:00:47,310
She's not a pushover.

17
00:00:48,440 --> 00:00:50,110
And I'm certainly not toying with her.

18
00:00:51,210 --> 00:00:52,450
If you'll just give me a chance,

19
00:00:54,010 --> 00:00:55,750
I'd like to try starting something with Seo Hyun.

20
00:00:57,280 --> 00:00:58,650
I heard you were seeing someone else.

21
00:01:00,190 --> 00:01:01,860
I heard the woman you couldn't forget...

22
00:01:01,920 --> 00:01:03,260
for eight years came back.

23
00:01:03,260 --> 00:01:04,460
What about her?

24
00:01:04,590 --> 00:01:05,590
Mom!

25
00:01:06,230 --> 00:01:07,630
It's over with her.

26
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:10,560
It ended eight years ago.

27
00:01:12,770 --> 00:01:13,770
So?

28
00:01:14,870 --> 00:01:16,470
Is my Seo Hyun just her replacement?

29
00:01:16,970 --> 00:01:18,840
Mom, what is wrong with you?

30
00:01:18,940 --> 00:01:19,970
It's not like that.

31
00:01:20,540 --> 00:01:23,380
You don't love her. You just pity her.

32
00:01:23,910 --> 00:01:24,910
You feel sorry for her,

33
00:01:24,980 --> 00:01:26,410
out of guilt and a sense of responsibility.

34
00:01:27,080 --> 00:01:30,350
So what if it's not love? So what if it's pity?

35
00:01:30,420 --> 00:01:31,550
Who cares if it's guilt,

36
00:01:31,620 --> 00:01:32,820
or if I'm just a rebound?

37
00:01:33,520 --> 00:01:34,590
Seo Hyun.

38
00:01:40,760 --> 00:01:43,830
I don't know what you're really thinking,

39
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:49,340
and even if you're only saying this on a whim,

40
00:01:50,240 --> 00:01:51,540
I don't care.

41
00:01:52,910 --> 00:01:53,940
I'm okay with it.

42
00:01:55,410 --> 00:01:56,540
I'm okay with all of it.

43
00:02:00,510 --> 00:02:03,750
Thank you for asking to be with me.

44
00:02:06,950 --> 00:02:08,050
Thank you so much.

45
00:02:41,090 --> 00:02:43,020
Mom, do you realise how strange you're being?

46
00:02:44,120 --> 00:02:45,730
You're the one being strange.

47
00:02:46,830 --> 00:02:48,360
Have you no self-respect?

48
00:02:50,030 --> 00:02:51,430
What do you think you're lacking?

49
00:02:52,030 --> 00:02:53,530
What's so wrong with you...

50
00:02:53,630 --> 00:02:55,400
that you'd debase yourself for a man who doesn't even love you?

51
00:02:56,270 --> 00:02:57,700
It's no better than begging.

52
00:02:58,170 --> 00:02:59,410
What on earth do you think you're doing?

53
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:01,370
What does self-respect have to do with love?

54
00:03:01,940 --> 00:03:03,780
If it means I can have him, what's wrong with begging a little?

55
00:03:04,340 --> 00:03:06,150
I would do even more than that.

56
00:03:06,580 --> 00:03:08,850
How can you say that in front of your mother...

57
00:03:10,950 --> 00:03:13,550
Do you think your father and I raised you...

58
00:03:13,890 --> 00:03:16,890
with such care just so you could be treated like this?

59
00:03:18,020 --> 00:03:20,390
I know I may seem pathetic and foolish to you,

60
00:03:20,660 --> 00:03:21,800
but this is me.

61
00:03:22,960 --> 00:03:25,430
I hate this about myself, and it's despicable,

62
00:03:25,730 --> 00:03:27,070
but this is who I am, Mom.

63
00:03:40,710 --> 00:03:41,720
Ms. Han.

64
00:03:42,380 --> 00:03:43,450
Ma'am, you're here.

65
00:03:44,680 --> 00:03:45,720
Ms. Han,

66
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:48,360
you shouldn't treat Heung Sik like that.

67
00:03:48,660 --> 00:03:50,520
What on earth did you say to him?

68
00:03:51,060 --> 00:03:54,490
He's just whimpering and sulking, and has taken to his bed.

69
00:03:56,730 --> 00:03:57,730
What was it?

70
00:03:58,370 --> 00:04:02,200
My goodness, this is so frustrating. Fill me in.

71
00:04:02,540 --> 00:04:04,270
Just a little while ago,

72
00:04:04,340 --> 00:04:07,040
he was perfectly fine, chewing on some squid.

73
00:04:07,270 --> 00:04:09,880
Then after your call, he suddenly...

74
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:13,150
collapsed like a leaf in a storm and took to his bed.

75
00:04:13,310 --> 00:04:14,810
This is your fault, isn't it?

76
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:18,390
Yes, you're right. It is my fault.

77
00:04:19,350 --> 00:04:22,220
So you finally went and told him.

78
00:04:23,060 --> 00:04:24,960
To a boy who isn't even fully healed.

79
00:04:25,260 --> 00:04:28,160
You really told him that Gyeol's Dad was back, didn't you?

80
00:04:28,260 --> 00:04:30,260
No, that's not it, Ma'am.

81
00:04:30,430 --> 00:04:31,430
Then what is it?

82
00:04:33,370 --> 00:04:35,400
Heung Sik hasn't given me an answer yet.

83
00:04:36,370 --> 00:04:39,310
When I hear his answer, I'll let you know right away, Ma'am.

84
00:04:40,170 --> 00:04:42,480
Fine. I see.

85
00:04:43,380 --> 00:04:45,850
So now that Gyeol's Dad is back,

86
00:04:45,850 --> 00:04:49,450
you told him to stop pestering you and to stay away.

87
00:04:50,180 --> 00:04:53,620
You drove a nail right through my Heung Sik's heart.

88
00:04:53,890 --> 00:04:55,960
Gyeol's Dad isn't here, Ma'am.

89
00:04:56,420 --> 00:04:57,590
Gyeol is my son.

90
00:04:57,660 --> 00:05:01,290
My goodness. I'm starting to see your true colours.

91
00:05:04,130 --> 00:05:06,530
He ended up like that trying to save your child.

92
00:05:06,530 --> 00:05:08,900
How could you be so cruel to my son?

93
00:05:09,570 --> 00:05:11,640
No matter how badly you wanted to or how urgent it was,

94
00:05:11,970 --> 00:05:15,640
you should have waited until the cast was off Heung Sik's arm.

95
00:05:16,710 --> 00:05:21,210
Does my Heung Sik need a cast for his heart now too?

96
00:05:24,580 --> 00:05:26,720
Are you sick, Gyu Rim?

97
00:05:28,890 --> 00:05:29,920
What's wrong with you,

98
00:05:29,990 --> 00:05:31,760
going around asking just anyone out like that?

99
00:05:31,830 --> 00:05:33,290
Don't you even know how scary men can be?

100
00:05:39,630 --> 00:05:40,630
What's this?

101
00:05:44,200 --> 00:05:45,470
A strapping young man...

102
00:05:45,470 --> 00:05:46,640
who could take down a bull with his bare hands...

103
00:05:46,640 --> 00:05:50,010
is lying here looking pathetic just because of a few words?

104
00:05:51,080 --> 00:05:52,710
Get up right now!

105
00:05:52,880 --> 00:05:55,550
Just leave me alone. I have things to think about.

106
00:05:55,620 --> 00:05:57,320
Think about what?

107
00:05:57,850 --> 00:06:00,650
Is Gyu Rim the only woman in the world?

108
00:06:01,220 --> 00:06:03,220
Just because I'm hung up on Gyu Rim,

109
00:06:03,290 --> 00:06:06,060
why are you hung up on her too?

110
00:06:06,060 --> 00:06:07,790
Don't you have your own type?

111
00:06:08,060 --> 00:06:09,200
Oh, come on.

112
00:06:09,860 --> 00:06:11,970
A man needs confidence, even if he's dying tomorrow.

113
00:06:11,970 --> 00:06:13,500
Ouch! That hurts.

114
00:06:14,030 --> 00:06:15,740
How can your hands sting that much?

115
00:06:16,370 --> 00:06:19,670
You may not have a decent job,

116
00:06:20,170 --> 00:06:22,080
and objectively, you don't really have...

117
00:06:22,140 --> 00:06:24,310
anything to show for yourself.

118
00:06:24,910 --> 00:06:28,150
But to me, you're the greatest son in the world.

119
00:06:29,450 --> 00:06:31,080
Bring me Chris Evans.

120
00:06:31,180 --> 00:06:32,850
I would never trade you for him. Not in a million years.

121
00:06:32,920 --> 00:06:35,160
That's not it, Mom.

122
00:06:35,220 --> 00:06:37,320
If it's not, then snap out of it, you punk.

123
00:06:37,390 --> 00:06:38,630
Stop looking so pathetic...

124
00:06:38,690 --> 00:06:40,390
in front of your mother who gave birth to you!

125
00:06:40,660 --> 00:06:44,600
Gyu Rim officially asked me to be with her.

126
00:06:44,660 --> 00:06:47,600
Right, Gyu Rim asked you to officially...

127
00:06:50,400 --> 00:06:51,400
Oh my goodness.

128
00:06:52,140 --> 00:06:56,010
Goodness, now you're talking nonsense, you brat.

129
00:06:57,140 --> 00:07:00,280
When that sign fell, did you hit your head too?

130
00:07:00,910 --> 00:07:02,280
How many fingers am I holding up?

131
00:07:03,150 --> 00:07:05,190
Gosh, three.

132
00:07:06,490 --> 00:07:09,390
I'm perfectly sane.

133
00:07:09,590 --> 00:07:12,330
Gyu Rim really did ask me out.

134
00:07:12,590 --> 00:07:14,290
Are you sure Gyu Rim isn't sick or something?

135
00:07:14,760 --> 00:07:16,300
Was Gyu Rim acting okay, Mom?

136
00:07:16,430 --> 00:07:20,570
So Gyu Rim really said she wants to date you?

137
00:07:20,970 --> 00:07:21,970
Yes.

138
00:07:29,340 --> 00:07:30,610
Oh, dear. What should I do?

139
00:07:32,510 --> 00:07:34,610
Why are you laughing one minute...

140
00:07:34,610 --> 00:07:35,720
and crying the next? You're scaring me.

141
00:07:36,720 --> 00:07:38,080
What am I going to do?

142
00:07:38,650 --> 00:07:40,950
Oh, I had no idea.

143
00:07:40,950 --> 00:07:43,120
I can't believe what I said to Gyu Rim.

144
00:07:43,920 --> 00:07:46,890
Gosh, what am I going to do with this big mouth of mine?

145
00:07:46,960 --> 00:07:49,160
- Oh, dear. - Why? What did you say?

146
00:07:49,660 --> 00:07:51,600
Are you crazy? What did you say?

147
00:07:51,970 --> 00:07:54,370
- What did you say to Gyu Rim? - I'm so embarrassed.

148
00:07:54,430 --> 00:07:57,470
This is driving me crazy. Seriously, what did you say?

149
00:07:57,540 --> 00:07:59,410
I don't know. What am I supposed to do?

150
00:08:16,490 --> 00:08:18,090
Son, what are you doing?

151
00:08:19,960 --> 00:08:21,690
If you're not busy, want to go on a date with Mom?

152
00:08:22,660 --> 00:08:24,530
(Damga Charcoal Grill)

153
00:08:28,970 --> 00:08:29,970
Is it good?

154
00:08:30,040 --> 00:08:31,500
Yes, it's delicious.

155
00:08:34,240 --> 00:08:35,440
Today,

156
00:08:35,610 --> 00:08:37,540
I asked Mr. Jo Heung Sik out.

157
00:08:38,440 --> 00:08:39,450
Really?

158
00:08:39,750 --> 00:08:43,180
But I haven't heard his answer yet. He might turn me down.

159
00:08:48,560 --> 00:08:49,660
Are you shocked?

160
00:08:51,820 --> 00:08:52,890
I'm a little surprised.

161
00:08:54,260 --> 00:08:55,260
But...

162
00:08:55,730 --> 00:08:57,300
are you doing this because of me?

163
00:08:58,870 --> 00:09:00,130
Because you're grateful that...

164
00:09:00,970 --> 00:09:02,570
Mr. Jo Heung Sik saved me?

165
00:09:03,070 --> 00:09:04,500
That's part of the reason.

166
00:09:05,740 --> 00:09:07,140
But it's not the only reason.

167
00:09:07,740 --> 00:09:08,780
Then what is it?

168
00:09:11,080 --> 00:09:13,110
I don't know when it started,

169
00:09:13,750 --> 00:09:16,220
but I've always felt a little cold.

170
00:09:17,180 --> 00:09:20,790
But when I'm with Ms. Park Su Nam and Mr. Jo Heung Sik,

171
00:09:21,390 --> 00:09:23,020
I feel so warm and happy.

172
00:09:23,360 --> 00:09:26,530
It's like finding spring in a winter blizzard.

173
00:09:26,930 --> 00:09:28,160
Really?

174
00:09:31,130 --> 00:09:33,100
But for such wonderful people,

175
00:09:33,100 --> 00:09:35,870
how could I be the one to upset them and make them cry?

176
00:09:36,640 --> 00:09:39,570
I should be doing everything I can to make them happy.

177
00:09:39,940 --> 00:09:41,340
I've been thinking about that.

178
00:09:41,740 --> 00:09:46,150
And I also told you that I wished I had a dad.

179
00:09:46,380 --> 00:09:48,380
Right, that's one of the reasons too.

180
00:09:48,720 --> 00:09:51,250
I see. That makes some sense.

181
00:09:52,720 --> 00:09:53,890
It does?

182
00:09:55,220 --> 00:09:56,220
To be honest,

183
00:09:56,490 --> 00:09:58,690
I was feeling very conflicted about it.

184
00:09:59,290 --> 00:10:01,030
But now that my son understands,

185
00:10:01,360 --> 00:10:02,900
it's such a relief.

186
00:10:03,730 --> 00:10:07,630
So are you going to marry Mr. Jo Heung Sik too?

187
00:10:07,830 --> 00:10:09,040
I don't know yet.

188
00:10:09,300 --> 00:10:11,370
He could still turn me down.

189
00:10:11,440 --> 00:10:13,810
No way. That will never happen.

190
00:10:14,040 --> 00:10:17,010
Mr. Jo Heung Sik likes you so much.

191
00:10:17,610 --> 00:10:21,780
If he says no, you tell me. I'll go have a word with him.

192
00:10:27,520 --> 00:10:28,760
Hey, Seo Hyun.

193
00:10:29,890 --> 00:10:31,660
You were taken aback by my mom, right?

194
00:10:31,920 --> 00:10:32,930
No.

195
00:10:34,230 --> 00:10:36,500
She was probably the one who was taken aback by me.

196
00:10:37,430 --> 00:10:38,870
And you must have been very surprised too.

197
00:10:41,500 --> 00:10:42,770
I'm not going to let you back out.

198
00:10:44,500 --> 00:10:45,970
Even if you call in an hour...

199
00:10:47,210 --> 00:10:48,880
and say you were just having a crazy moment...

200
00:10:49,140 --> 00:10:51,010
and ask to take back your confession,

201
00:10:51,180 --> 00:10:52,650
I'm not letting you back out.

202
00:10:55,480 --> 00:10:59,290
- Okay. - Or if you changed your mind...

203
00:10:59,620 --> 00:11:01,250
and ask me to pretend I didn't hear you,

204
00:11:01,320 --> 00:11:02,560
I'm not letting you back out.

205
00:11:04,620 --> 00:11:05,660
Okay.

206
00:11:05,660 --> 00:11:07,160
Or if you think it over and decide...

207
00:11:07,160 --> 00:11:09,630
you can't forget Han Gyu Rim and you cry and beg,

208
00:11:09,860 --> 00:11:11,260
I'm still not letting you back out.

209
00:11:13,070 --> 00:11:14,070
Okay.

210
00:11:14,200 --> 00:11:16,070
There's no turning back now.

211
00:11:18,270 --> 00:11:20,970
- Okay. - No take-backs.

212
00:11:23,680 --> 00:11:24,680
There.

213
00:11:24,980 --> 00:11:28,310
I just wanted to make sure. That's why I called.

214
00:11:29,580 --> 00:11:31,180
See you again tomorrow.

215
00:11:32,290 --> 00:11:33,290
Yes.

216
00:11:34,650 --> 00:11:35,920
Okay, sleep well.

217
00:12:14,090 --> 00:12:15,090
What's this?

218
00:12:15,930 --> 00:12:18,460
Earthlings call this a "cake."

219
00:12:19,870 --> 00:12:21,030
Is today my birthday?

220
00:12:22,540 --> 00:12:23,540
Is it your birthday?

221
00:12:24,070 --> 00:12:25,970
You can't even remember your own birthday or mine,

222
00:12:25,970 --> 00:12:27,440
you thoughtless jerk.

223
00:12:28,310 --> 00:12:29,510
Here, hold this.

224
00:12:35,250 --> 00:12:37,420
To day one. Congratulations.

225
00:12:37,950 --> 00:12:39,320
Blow them out. I want to take a picture.

226
00:12:39,450 --> 00:12:40,450
What is this?

227
00:12:41,050 --> 00:12:42,190
Are we dating now?

228
00:12:43,190 --> 00:12:44,460
Because I'm really not into you.

229
00:12:44,520 --> 00:12:47,030
Are you crazy? I'm not into you either.

230
00:12:47,090 --> 00:12:49,700
You said you agreed to date Seo Hyun.

231
00:12:55,700 --> 00:12:57,100
The candles are melting, man.

232
00:12:57,170 --> 00:12:58,240
I had to beg them to sell me this last night...

233
00:12:58,240 --> 00:12:59,640
as they were closing.

234
00:13:02,240 --> 00:13:03,810
Oh, for goodness' sake.

235
00:13:10,620 --> 00:13:11,620
You did the right thing.

236
00:13:12,080 --> 00:13:13,350
You absolutely did the right thing.

237
00:13:13,550 --> 00:13:17,090
A relationship doesn't have to start with a fiery passion on both sides.

238
00:13:17,190 --> 00:13:19,690
Feelings can grow as you date someone.

239
00:13:21,560 --> 00:13:22,760
That's enough.

240
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:27,200
You ended things well...

241
00:13:28,600 --> 00:13:29,840
with Han Gyu Rim, right?

242
00:13:35,410 --> 00:13:37,410
Did you end things properly with Gyu Rim?

243
00:13:38,880 --> 00:13:40,210
When did I ever...

244
00:13:41,750 --> 00:13:43,180
start anything with Gyu Rim?

245
00:13:44,620 --> 00:13:45,620
That's true.

246
00:13:46,590 --> 00:13:48,120
You never even got to start.

247
00:13:51,290 --> 00:13:52,460
Anyway,

248
00:13:52,890 --> 00:13:53,960
all it took was you changing your mind,

249
00:13:54,030 --> 00:13:55,800
and now everyone's happy.

250
00:14:02,270 --> 00:14:03,470
Is that really true?

251
00:14:05,040 --> 00:14:06,170
What is?

252
00:14:07,970 --> 00:14:09,680
That everyone is happy.

253
00:14:10,640 --> 00:14:11,880
Is that really true?

254
00:14:23,320 --> 00:14:24,920
Why do you keep laughing?

255
00:14:25,760 --> 00:14:27,290
Me? When?

256
00:14:27,590 --> 00:14:28,690
Just now.

257
00:14:29,400 --> 00:14:32,270
- What? - Earlier, in the shower,

258
00:14:32,500 --> 00:14:34,130
you were laughing out loud.

259
00:14:34,330 --> 00:14:36,440
I could hear you all the way out here.

260
00:14:37,070 --> 00:14:38,740
I don't think I did that.

261
00:14:38,870 --> 00:14:40,070
Did I?

262
00:14:40,440 --> 00:14:42,710
Do you have no pride either?

263
00:14:43,380 --> 00:14:46,310
After all the heartache Mu Jin caused our Seo Hyun,

264
00:14:46,610 --> 00:14:49,550
you just let it go so easily and laugh about it.

265
00:14:50,820 --> 00:14:53,120
Are you really Seo Hyun's father?

266
00:14:54,650 --> 00:14:55,660
Oh my.

267
00:14:55,960 --> 00:14:58,120
There you go, laughing again.

268
00:15:00,460 --> 00:15:02,400
I can't stand Mu Jin.

269
00:15:03,200 --> 00:15:05,560
He could be the last man on Earth, and I still wouldn't approve.

270
00:15:05,830 --> 00:15:10,670
Honestly, how can a man's feelings change at the drop of a hat?

271
00:15:11,270 --> 00:15:13,810
How do we know when he'll change his mind again?

272
00:15:14,310 --> 00:15:15,370
Goodness.

273
00:15:15,610 --> 00:15:18,480
If that brat breaks Seo Hyun's heart again...

274
00:15:18,540 --> 00:15:19,850
I swear, this time...

275
00:15:21,350 --> 00:15:22,350
Honey.

276
00:15:22,720 --> 00:15:25,790
Are you holding back a laugh?

277
00:15:27,950 --> 00:15:29,360
Honey.

278
00:15:31,260 --> 00:15:33,860
You know, seeing you get all worked up...

279
00:15:33,930 --> 00:15:35,460
and cussing someone out and getting angry...

280
00:15:35,530 --> 00:15:37,730
is a first for me since we met.

281
00:15:38,900 --> 00:15:40,170
So you find that funny?

282
00:15:40,570 --> 00:15:43,700
So me getting all worked up and angry is funny to you?

283
00:15:43,970 --> 00:15:45,840
No, it's not that it's funny.

284
00:15:46,940 --> 00:15:49,340
I'm grateful. Okay?

285
00:15:50,480 --> 00:15:51,580
Okay...

286
00:15:52,110 --> 00:15:55,080
I find the fact that you're so upset for Seo Hyun's sake...

287
00:15:55,450 --> 00:15:56,650
beautiful,

288
00:15:57,250 --> 00:15:59,890
and I'm so grateful for it. You know?

289
00:16:00,390 --> 00:16:02,760
What is this man talking about?

290
00:16:02,820 --> 00:16:04,420
Do you know how adorable you are?

291
00:16:07,130 --> 00:16:08,790
Oh, honey.

292
00:16:09,260 --> 00:16:12,570
Sometimes, I feel like I'm the fake father,

293
00:16:12,630 --> 00:16:16,100
and you're Seo Hyun's real mother. I do.

294
00:16:20,240 --> 00:16:23,040
- What are you talking about? - What?

295
00:16:23,980 --> 00:16:25,750
I am Seo Hyun's mother.

296
00:16:27,010 --> 00:16:29,280
I may not have given birth to her,

297
00:16:30,120 --> 00:16:34,790
but from the moment I married you, Seo Hyun has been my child.

298
00:16:35,250 --> 00:16:38,120
I know. Of course, I know that.

299
00:16:38,660 --> 00:16:40,130
Then why would you say that?

300
00:16:42,230 --> 00:16:43,500
Getting upset and angry...

301
00:16:43,560 --> 00:16:45,100
because you're worried your child will be hurt...

302
00:16:45,160 --> 00:16:46,470
is only natural for a mother.

303
00:16:47,030 --> 00:16:49,700
What's so beautiful or worth being grateful for about that?

304
00:16:50,770 --> 00:16:52,610
What on earth do you take me for?

305
00:16:52,810 --> 00:16:55,940
- How could you say that? - Honey.

306
00:16:56,980 --> 00:16:59,610
No, that's not what I meant...

307
00:17:01,880 --> 00:17:04,020
Oh, I'm sorry. That was thoughtless of me.

308
00:17:04,250 --> 00:17:05,520
I'm truly sorry.

309
00:17:07,620 --> 00:17:09,590
Oh, Yoon Hee. Yoon Hee.

310
00:17:10,390 --> 00:17:11,460
Please, listen to me.

311
00:17:12,690 --> 00:17:14,560
That's not what I was trying to say.

312
00:17:15,590 --> 00:17:16,600
It's just...

313
00:17:17,730 --> 00:17:19,800
Can I become a good father...

314
00:17:20,170 --> 00:17:22,000
with your children?

315
00:17:24,670 --> 00:17:27,740
Gyu Rim, Gyu Young, and Gyu Oh, right?

316
00:17:28,840 --> 00:17:30,140
It's a little late,

317
00:17:30,840 --> 00:17:33,980
but I want to start acting like a father to them, too.

318
00:17:34,550 --> 00:17:36,880
Could you give me that chance?

319
00:17:39,820 --> 00:17:40,820
Can you?

320
00:17:59,110 --> 00:18:00,540
Don't scold me.

321
00:18:01,510 --> 00:18:04,010
I just checked my blood pressure, and it was 160.

322
00:18:04,810 --> 00:18:07,280
And putting cucumbers on your face lowers blood pressure?

323
00:18:07,810 --> 00:18:11,080
There are some cucumbers left, so you should come put some on.

324
00:18:11,480 --> 00:18:12,720
As for the laundry,

325
00:18:12,790 --> 00:18:14,950
I'll fold it later when my blood pressure goes down.

326
00:18:16,060 --> 00:18:17,060
It's fine.

327
00:18:17,690 --> 00:18:20,530
Come on, I'm telling you to come take care of your skin.

328
00:18:21,430 --> 00:18:23,330
Gyu Young's wedding is less than a month away.

329
00:18:25,030 --> 00:18:27,200
Just give up on Gyu Young's wedding, Dad.

330
00:18:27,570 --> 00:18:29,500
Her future husband's family thinks you passed away...

331
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:31,500
I'm not dead.

332
00:18:32,670 --> 00:18:34,470
I have been resurrected.

333
00:18:36,640 --> 00:18:40,710
After Gyu Young thought about it, she realised she needed her father.

334
00:18:41,110 --> 00:18:43,250
She begged me for forgiveness.

335
00:18:44,050 --> 00:18:45,220
She said she was wrong...

336
00:18:45,480 --> 00:18:47,320
and pleaded with me to come to the wedding...

337
00:18:47,820 --> 00:18:50,360
while shedding these big, fat tears.

338
00:18:51,060 --> 00:18:52,160
Gyu Young did?

339
00:18:52,360 --> 00:18:54,130
Yes. I...

340
00:18:54,330 --> 00:18:55,730
It's falling off, darn it.

341
00:18:55,930 --> 00:18:59,170
You know I have a real soft spot for people who need me, right?

342
00:18:59,870 --> 00:19:02,570
I was going to say, "I don't have a daughter like you,"

343
00:19:02,640 --> 00:19:03,900
and just completely ignore her.

344
00:19:04,200 --> 00:19:05,440
But I'm still her father.

345
00:19:05,500 --> 00:19:07,970
How could I do the same to her? Right?

346
00:19:09,310 --> 00:19:12,110
So you should just pretend to give in...

347
00:19:12,950 --> 00:19:14,510
and come with me. Okay?

348
00:19:17,580 --> 00:19:18,620
Darn it.

349
00:19:19,720 --> 00:19:20,750
Gyu Rim,

350
00:19:21,250 --> 00:19:23,020
just be the one to give in. All right?

351
00:19:23,260 --> 00:19:24,720
You're the eldest, after all.

352
00:19:25,860 --> 00:19:26,990
Goodness.

353
00:19:38,170 --> 00:19:39,170
You startled me.

354
00:19:39,310 --> 00:19:40,840
I almost pierced my ear in the wrong place.

355
00:19:40,840 --> 00:19:42,740
- Don't you know how to knock? - What is going on?

356
00:19:43,510 --> 00:19:45,280
Did you tell your future husband's family the truth about Dad?

357
00:19:45,680 --> 00:19:47,410
He said you asked him to come to your wedding.

358
00:19:47,580 --> 00:19:48,610
As if.

359
00:19:48,950 --> 00:19:50,580
Dad's the one who took a joke way too seriously.

360
00:19:50,780 --> 00:19:52,690
You lied to Dad?

361
00:19:53,190 --> 00:19:55,590
It wasn't a lie. It was a joke. A joke.

362
00:19:58,390 --> 00:19:59,930
That's not something to joke about.

363
00:20:00,290 --> 00:20:01,760
Do you have any idea how excited Dad is...

364
00:20:01,760 --> 00:20:03,030
about going to your wedding?

365
00:20:03,860 --> 00:20:06,600
Well, you can calm him down for me. Now, give me the earrings.

366
00:20:06,970 --> 00:20:09,100
You made this mess, so you clean it up.

367
00:20:09,170 --> 00:20:11,370
Give me the earrings. I have to get to work.

368
00:20:11,540 --> 00:20:13,470
Fix this first, then go to work.

369
00:20:14,410 --> 00:20:16,380
It's not like Dad did what I asked him to do, either.

370
00:20:16,710 --> 00:20:18,140
What did you ask Dad to do?

371
00:20:20,150 --> 00:20:22,180
What did you ask Dad to do?

372
00:20:24,720 --> 00:20:27,220
I told him to tell Su Nam and the Rice Thief,

373
00:20:27,990 --> 00:20:29,760
Jo Heung Sik, that Gyeol's Dad was back. Why?

374
00:20:33,260 --> 00:20:34,390
You told him to do that?

375
00:20:34,530 --> 00:20:37,160
That's right, I did. To break you and Jo Heung Sik up.

376
00:20:37,400 --> 00:20:38,400
Why?

377
00:20:39,530 --> 00:20:40,870
Because he keeps meddling in my affairs and threatening me...

378
00:20:40,930 --> 00:20:42,230
all because of you.

379
00:20:43,570 --> 00:20:46,370
So you're the one who dragged Mrs. Park into this.

380
00:20:46,810 --> 00:20:50,010
- What? - Who are you, hurting good people?

381
00:20:50,480 --> 00:20:52,140
If it weren't for those two,

382
00:20:52,510 --> 00:20:54,550
our family wouldn't have made it this far.

383
00:20:55,310 --> 00:20:56,550
What gives you the right?

384
00:20:57,350 --> 00:20:58,550
What gives me the right?

385
00:20:58,780 --> 00:20:59,790
Unbelievable.

386
00:21:07,160 --> 00:21:11,460
Hi, it's Gyeol. Mister, how are you feeling today?

387
00:21:11,760 --> 00:21:13,100
I'm feeling a whole lot better.

388
00:21:13,370 --> 00:21:15,230
I'll be getting this cast off soon too.

389
00:21:15,770 --> 00:21:16,870
That's a relief.

390
00:21:17,100 --> 00:21:18,940
It wasn't a serious injury to begin with.

391
00:21:19,270 --> 00:21:21,610
You really don't have to worry so much.

392
00:21:21,810 --> 00:21:23,210
Mister, by the way,

393
00:21:23,740 --> 00:21:27,010
is it true my mom asked to be with you?

394
00:21:27,580 --> 00:21:29,620
Gyeol, how do you know about that?

395
00:21:31,150 --> 00:21:33,450
- No way. - My mom told me.

396
00:21:34,120 --> 00:21:36,860
She said she's waiting for your answer.

397
00:21:37,490 --> 00:21:40,790
So, when are you going to answer her?

398
00:21:41,490 --> 00:21:42,530
Will it take a long time?

399
00:21:43,160 --> 00:21:44,500
How long will it take?

400
00:21:45,630 --> 00:21:48,030
Well, you see... It's just...

401
00:21:48,870 --> 00:21:52,870
Should I even dare to give an answer or not?

402
00:21:52,940 --> 00:21:55,170
Whether I have the right to or not.

403
00:21:58,610 --> 00:22:00,280
Can't you do it a little sooner?

404
00:22:01,350 --> 00:22:05,950
You need to answer soon so I can make my decision soon too.

405
00:22:06,920 --> 00:22:11,360
So will you accept my mom's feelings or not?

406
00:22:11,420 --> 00:22:14,460
Can't you at least give me the odds?

407
00:22:15,690 --> 00:22:16,700
The odds?

408
00:22:18,660 --> 00:22:21,400
Hey, what are you even asking? It's a hundred to zero, obviously.

409
00:22:21,600 --> 00:22:23,400
Hey, Han Gyu Oh, what are you doing?

410
00:22:23,470 --> 00:22:25,270
That's my call. Put the phone to my ear!

411
00:22:27,240 --> 00:22:29,540
Hey, Han Gyeol, you're so cool.

412
00:22:30,240 --> 00:22:31,240
How so?

413
00:22:31,680 --> 00:22:33,010
I mean, I thought if your mom got a boyfriend,

414
00:22:33,080 --> 00:22:34,480
you'd tell her to break up with him immediately,

415
00:22:34,910 --> 00:22:38,450
and throw a tantrum, begging her to focus only on you.

416
00:22:39,490 --> 00:22:41,320
I'm so surprised by how cool and awesome you are.

417
00:22:41,520 --> 00:22:42,820
I suppose I am.

418
00:22:45,290 --> 00:22:47,160
(Children Who Benefit the World)

419
00:22:48,160 --> 00:22:50,060
I have to get to class. Bye.

420
00:22:53,270 --> 00:22:56,340
Tell Mr. Jo Heung Sik I'll call him again.

421
00:23:06,780 --> 00:23:08,010
Mu Jin and Seo Hyun?

422
00:23:08,650 --> 00:23:09,650
Since when?

423
00:23:09,650 --> 00:23:11,450
(Chairman Hong Ok Seon)

424
00:23:11,450 --> 00:23:13,420
But Yoon Hee is strongly against it.

425
00:23:13,920 --> 00:23:14,950
Yoon Hee is?

426
00:23:16,490 --> 00:23:20,130
Well, Mu Jin did cause Seo Hyun a lot of heartache.

427
00:23:21,190 --> 00:23:23,300
But as they say, no parent can win against their child.

428
00:23:23,730 --> 00:23:25,930
My gosh. You're one to talk.

429
00:23:26,400 --> 00:23:29,640
After all this time you spent railroading your kids.

430
00:23:31,100 --> 00:23:34,170
Chairman Jang, what about you? Are you against Mu Jin too?

431
00:23:34,410 --> 00:23:35,410
Me?

432
00:23:36,140 --> 00:23:37,140
Well...

433
00:23:37,680 --> 00:23:39,680
Well, Seo Hyun likes him.

434
00:23:40,410 --> 00:23:42,150
Whether I was annoyed with him in the past or not,

435
00:23:42,210 --> 00:23:44,580
I just hope the two of them can be happy together.

436
00:23:45,980 --> 00:23:47,020
I don't know.

437
00:23:47,790 --> 00:23:50,520
If Yoon Hee keeps opposing it, it'll be hard for me.

438
00:23:51,220 --> 00:23:52,220
Listen...

439
00:23:52,790 --> 00:23:54,960
Hey, Chairman Jang, are you and Yoon Hee...

440
00:23:54,960 --> 00:23:55,960
free this evening?

441
00:23:56,830 --> 00:24:00,570
I was thinking we could have dinner, and I could talk to Yoon Hee.

442
00:24:01,600 --> 00:24:03,800
Yes. Chairman Jang, you talk to her for me. Okay?

443
00:24:04,340 --> 00:24:05,570
I'm counting on you, my friend.

444
00:24:05,640 --> 00:24:08,370
(Chairman Hong Ok Seon)

445
00:24:15,280 --> 00:24:16,280
Are you busy?

446
00:24:18,020 --> 00:24:22,590
Is it true that Mu Jin asked Seo Hyun to date him?

447
00:24:23,060 --> 00:24:26,020
He asked Seo Hyun right in front of Yoon Hee for her blessing.

448
00:24:27,260 --> 00:24:28,390
What about Han Gyu Rim?

449
00:24:30,430 --> 00:24:31,460
What about his son?

450
00:24:31,530 --> 00:24:32,530
Be quiet.

451
00:24:34,500 --> 00:24:36,940
We're not even sure if he's Mu Jin's son,

452
00:24:37,000 --> 00:24:38,000
so be quiet.

453
00:24:39,440 --> 00:24:41,010
Should I stop looking into it, then?

454
00:24:42,910 --> 00:24:44,040
Put it on hold for now.

455
00:24:44,980 --> 00:24:48,150
Nothing good will come of it if Seo Hyun's family finds out.

456
00:24:48,510 --> 00:24:50,050
We can't just pour cold water on them...

457
00:24:50,120 --> 00:24:51,380
when they've barely just begun.

458
00:24:53,050 --> 00:24:54,490
There's no such thing as a secret in this world.

459
00:24:54,950 --> 00:24:57,820
Even if they find out eventually, now is not the time.

460
00:25:24,650 --> 00:25:25,720
This is the last order, right?

461
00:25:25,780 --> 00:25:27,790
Yes, Chef. I've really learned a lot.

462
00:25:27,990 --> 00:25:29,020
Thank you for everything, Chef.

463
00:25:45,300 --> 00:25:47,140
What's with that look? You're creeping me out.

464
00:25:48,170 --> 00:25:49,370
There's a customer.

465
00:25:54,880 --> 00:25:56,380
We're about to go on break. What customer?

466
00:25:56,450 --> 00:25:57,650
A customer for you.

467
00:25:58,620 --> 00:26:01,450
You guys go ahead and eat and rest as planned.

468
00:26:01,620 --> 00:26:03,660
You guys don't even wait to hear the whole thing.

469
00:26:07,190 --> 00:26:08,190
Who is it?

470
00:26:16,770 --> 00:26:18,100
There are no straws.

471
00:26:21,410 --> 00:26:22,410
Okay.

472
00:26:37,560 --> 00:26:38,790
What brings you here?

473
00:26:41,460 --> 00:26:42,530
I took a taxi.

474
00:26:45,000 --> 00:26:47,030
Is there something you wanted to say to me?

475
00:26:47,630 --> 00:26:50,540
I have something to say, and something to ask.

476
00:26:53,070 --> 00:26:54,070
Well...

477
00:26:55,070 --> 00:26:56,310
To be honest,

478
00:26:57,140 --> 00:26:58,610
I'm not Gyu Rim's husband.

479
00:27:00,450 --> 00:27:02,350
Yes, I know that.

480
00:27:02,750 --> 00:27:03,750
You know?

481
00:27:04,280 --> 00:27:05,380
Did Gyu Rim tell you?

482
00:27:06,050 --> 00:27:07,090
Is that important?

483
00:27:08,050 --> 00:27:10,560
Well, no, that's not important.

484
00:27:12,760 --> 00:27:14,030
But Gyu Rim...

485
00:27:14,490 --> 00:27:18,560
asked me out yesterday.

486
00:27:20,130 --> 00:27:22,430
What, did you come here to brag?

487
00:27:22,630 --> 00:27:24,640
I didn't come here to brag.

488
00:27:26,200 --> 00:27:27,340
It's just...

489
00:27:31,880 --> 00:27:33,210
Oh, here...

490
00:27:48,690 --> 00:27:50,530
Is it okay if I date Gyu Rim?

491
00:27:53,830 --> 00:27:55,830
I wanted to see if there was any chance...

492
00:27:55,900 --> 00:27:57,940
you and Gyu Rim might get back together.

493
00:27:58,400 --> 00:28:00,370
That's what I came here to find out.

494
00:28:00,540 --> 00:28:01,540
No.

495
00:28:02,110 --> 00:28:03,540
That was a fast answer.

496
00:28:03,980 --> 00:28:07,110
- You didn't hear it correctly. - No.

497
00:28:07,910 --> 00:28:10,120
Hey, don't just keep saying no.

498
00:28:10,880 --> 00:28:13,620
- I'll ask you again, slowly. - No.

499
00:28:13,690 --> 00:28:16,790
Hey, don't do something you'll regret later.

500
00:28:17,560 --> 00:28:18,790
I'm going to count to ten,

501
00:28:19,090 --> 00:28:21,360
so think about it carefully and then answer me.

502
00:28:22,490 --> 00:28:23,830
- One. - No.

503
00:28:24,900 --> 00:28:26,570
There's absolutely no chance we'll get back together.

504
00:28:29,530 --> 00:28:31,140
Can you really cut...

505
00:28:31,470 --> 00:28:33,970
your feelings so cleanly, just like that?

506
00:28:34,970 --> 00:28:36,880
So what is it you want to hear from me?

507
00:28:37,140 --> 00:28:40,650
An honest answer. All right? Put your hand on your heart,

508
00:28:41,310 --> 00:28:42,480
look up to the sky,

509
00:28:42,680 --> 00:28:45,650
and give me an honest answer, with nothing to be ashamed of.

510
00:28:47,450 --> 00:28:49,320
I've already told you no several times,

511
00:28:49,420 --> 00:28:51,020
but you don't seem to be getting the message.

512
00:28:52,190 --> 00:28:53,390
I'm a bit busy today.

513
00:28:54,430 --> 00:28:55,960
You should go. I'll call a taxi for you.

514
00:28:56,860 --> 00:28:57,860
Would you like some more?

515
00:29:05,140 --> 00:29:07,310
So he's really saying no?

516
00:29:07,570 --> 00:29:08,570
Please get up.

517
00:29:08,640 --> 00:29:12,510
That's great. You know what?

518
00:29:13,010 --> 00:29:17,020
This is a great way to relieve three days of pent-up stress.

519
00:29:18,150 --> 00:29:19,790
Doesn't the owner complain that I come so often...

520
00:29:19,850 --> 00:29:21,420
without even buying anything?

521
00:29:21,590 --> 00:29:23,560
Not at all. You can come every day.

522
00:29:25,220 --> 00:29:27,030
Manager Song, talk to Gyu Rim for me.

523
00:29:27,430 --> 00:29:28,990
Tell her to put this in her father's room.

524
00:29:29,060 --> 00:29:32,430
- Just mention it casually. - Okay.

525
00:29:34,000 --> 00:29:35,270
Goodness.

526
00:29:35,400 --> 00:29:36,900
I'm going to lose my mind. Right?

527
00:29:37,370 --> 00:29:39,540
After causing such a ridiculous mess,

528
00:29:39,600 --> 00:29:42,510
look at you just lying there without a care in the world.

529
00:29:42,570 --> 00:29:46,280
Get up right now. You hear me? I'm about to grab you by the collar.

530
00:29:46,510 --> 00:29:49,350
Hey, why would you grab my collar, ma'am?

531
00:29:49,820 --> 00:29:51,380
Do you own my collar or something?

532
00:29:51,620 --> 00:29:53,550
What did you tell me yesterday?

533
00:29:54,150 --> 00:29:57,090
That Gyeol's Dad appeared?

534
00:29:57,520 --> 00:29:59,990
And that Gyeol's Mom and my Heung Sik...

535
00:30:00,060 --> 00:30:01,560
should just go their separate ways.

536
00:30:01,630 --> 00:30:03,130
Did you say that or not?

537
00:30:03,760 --> 00:30:06,900
What kind of grudge do you have against me...

538
00:30:06,970 --> 00:30:09,330
to tell such a terrible lie?

539
00:30:10,670 --> 00:30:11,800
Why do you say it's a lie?

540
00:30:12,370 --> 00:30:13,610
Do you have any proof that it's a lie?

541
00:30:13,670 --> 00:30:16,240
Proof? Proof...

542
00:30:16,810 --> 00:30:21,510
If what you're saying is true, then why would Gyeol's Mom...

543
00:30:21,580 --> 00:30:24,080
ask my Heung Sik out?

544
00:30:24,620 --> 00:30:26,720
Why don't you answer that first?

545
00:30:27,250 --> 00:30:30,090
Do you think my Han Gyu Rim is the kind of person...

546
00:30:30,160 --> 00:30:32,860
who would two-time somebody?

547
00:30:34,290 --> 00:30:35,330
Darn it.

548
00:30:36,860 --> 00:30:40,400
What did you say? My Gyu Rim asked him out?

549
00:30:40,500 --> 00:30:44,300
- Hey, wait. Stop this thing. - Yes, sir.

550
00:30:44,800 --> 00:30:47,810
So, you're not saying she was the one who was asked out,

551
00:30:47,870 --> 00:30:49,570
but that Gyu Rim asked him first?

552
00:30:50,480 --> 00:30:52,180
Ma'am, are you sure you're not lying?

553
00:30:53,250 --> 00:30:57,680
If you really don't believe me, go ask Gyeol's Mom yourself. Okay?

554
00:31:01,290 --> 00:31:04,490
What has gotten into them lately?

555
00:31:05,020 --> 00:31:06,990
Why is everyone acting so strange?

556
00:31:07,130 --> 00:31:09,490
Considering all the heartache I've been through,

557
00:31:09,590 --> 00:31:12,560
I really have to take it out on someone.

558
00:31:13,160 --> 00:31:14,270
How should I do it?

559
00:31:15,000 --> 00:31:19,740
Yes. A few months ago, you got drunk in broad daylight...

560
00:31:19,800 --> 00:31:23,780
and peed on the wall over there. The neighbours...

561
00:31:23,940 --> 00:31:26,650
Oh, good grief. Why are you being like this?

562
00:31:26,710 --> 00:31:27,710
Seriously.

563
00:31:27,780 --> 00:31:29,310
- Let go of this. - Oh my.

564
00:31:30,280 --> 00:31:32,180
You seem to have too much energy, ma'am.

565
00:31:32,180 --> 00:31:35,420
I have more than enough energy to take my anger out on you.

566
00:31:35,650 --> 00:31:36,690
Oh, darn it.

567
00:31:50,240 --> 00:31:51,400
My makeup is a mess, darn it...

568
00:31:55,640 --> 00:31:57,380
I'm Han Gyu Young. My name is Han Gyu Young.

569
00:31:57,440 --> 00:31:58,440
I'm Han Gyu Young.

570
00:31:59,680 --> 00:32:01,080
Why are they taking so long?

571
00:32:02,150 --> 00:32:03,350
When are they going to get here?

572
00:32:04,380 --> 00:32:06,020
Darn it...

573
00:32:06,650 --> 00:32:07,690
Darn it.

574
00:32:07,750 --> 00:32:09,450
How can none of them be winners?

575
00:32:11,060 --> 00:32:12,420
The great Han Gyu Young,

576
00:32:12,520 --> 00:32:15,030
how did you stoop to scratching lottery tickets?

577
00:32:28,670 --> 00:32:31,740
I'm sorry to have kept you waiting. I'm Kim Yoon Jin.

578
00:32:34,180 --> 00:32:36,180
I need to get new business cards made.

579
00:32:36,280 --> 00:32:37,550
My name is Han Gyu Young.

580
00:32:38,780 --> 00:32:39,780
Han Gyu Young.

581
00:32:41,750 --> 00:32:43,420
I know someone with a similar name.

582
00:32:45,690 --> 00:32:47,630
Really? What's her name?

583
00:32:48,990 --> 00:32:50,560
The name is similar,

584
00:32:51,360 --> 00:32:53,430
but she's a completely different person from you, Gyu Young.

585
00:32:55,230 --> 00:32:56,330
Oh, by the way,

586
00:32:56,400 --> 00:32:57,840
you had an interesting idea.

587
00:32:58,640 --> 00:33:01,240
That's why I begged them to let me meet with you.

588
00:33:03,910 --> 00:33:05,440
No matter how well you do your makeup,

589
00:33:05,510 --> 00:33:07,980
it oxidizes and breaks down over time, right?

590
00:33:08,210 --> 00:33:10,250
That's why everyone is so obsessed with touching it up.

591
00:33:10,820 --> 00:33:12,450
That's because, in the first place, the skincare...

592
00:33:12,520 --> 00:33:14,690
isn't creating a proper base for the skin.

593
00:33:15,050 --> 00:33:16,990
If you just get the skin's condition right,

594
00:33:17,290 --> 00:33:18,690
the makeup will last longer, won't it?

595
00:33:19,290 --> 00:33:22,430
Looking pretty all day long, that's the real game changer.

596
00:33:23,930 --> 00:33:24,930
I like it.

597
00:33:27,970 --> 00:33:29,970
I guess true geniuses are just born different.

598
00:33:31,070 --> 00:33:32,300
I feel inadequate.

599
00:33:38,010 --> 00:33:39,410
Let's work together.

600
00:33:39,510 --> 00:33:41,610
I'll give you our full, unstinting support,

601
00:33:41,680 --> 00:33:42,680
and I'll give you the best...

602
00:33:42,750 --> 00:33:43,750
compensation package in the industry.

603
00:33:45,480 --> 00:33:46,480
Thank you.

604
00:33:46,580 --> 00:33:47,920
I'll work hard.

605
00:33:48,450 --> 00:33:49,520
Please do.

606
00:33:49,650 --> 00:33:50,660
Okay.

607
00:34:01,770 --> 00:34:03,030
Darn it...

608
00:34:05,740 --> 00:34:08,170
- Yes, Mother. - Gyu Young.

609
00:34:08,240 --> 00:34:09,840
I'm not calling at a bad time, am I?

610
00:34:09,910 --> 00:34:12,110
Oh, not at all. I was just taking a short break.

611
00:34:12,680 --> 00:34:15,880
I should have called you first. I'm sorry, Mother.

612
00:34:17,050 --> 00:34:18,480
No, it's fine.

613
00:34:18,680 --> 00:34:21,450
The wedding is less than a month away,

614
00:34:21,650 --> 00:34:24,220
and with the preparations and the gifts...

615
00:34:24,360 --> 00:34:26,360
I was just wondering how everything was coming along.

616
00:34:26,520 --> 00:34:29,790
Yes, I'm working hard to prepare everything well.

617
00:34:29,860 --> 00:34:32,200
Listen, both your family and mine...

618
00:34:32,260 --> 00:34:34,700
have a certain social and economic standing.

619
00:34:34,770 --> 00:34:37,070
Isn't it a bit too frugal?

620
00:34:37,240 --> 00:34:40,340
You know everyone is thinking that, right?

621
00:34:40,840 --> 00:34:43,980
Exactly. You said it yourself, Mother,

622
00:34:44,080 --> 00:34:46,240
that leaders of society must set an example.

623
00:34:46,310 --> 00:34:48,210
You're absolutely right, Mother.

624
00:34:48,710 --> 00:34:50,350
Oh, and I was looking at the list again,

625
00:34:50,450 --> 00:34:52,180
and I noticed the fourth uncle's wife was missing.

626
00:34:52,480 --> 00:34:53,650
Originally,

627
00:34:54,590 --> 00:34:57,920
she and the fourth uncle were divorced, but my goodness,

628
00:34:57,990 --> 00:34:59,590
they got back together two weeks ago.

629
00:34:59,860 --> 00:35:02,060
Anyway, she'll be upset if we leave her out,

630
00:35:02,260 --> 00:35:06,300
so let's get one more alligator bag for her.

631
00:35:06,600 --> 00:35:10,140
- Is that all right? - Oh, of course. That's fine.

632
00:35:10,270 --> 00:35:12,870
Gyu Young, have a wonderful day.

633
00:35:13,000 --> 00:35:15,110
Yes, you too, Mother...

634
00:35:22,950 --> 00:35:24,520
I'd like to cancel my instalment savings account.

635
00:35:25,680 --> 00:35:28,790
Ma'am, it matures in three months.

636
00:35:28,790 --> 00:35:31,020
Yes, I know that better than anyone,

637
00:35:31,090 --> 00:35:32,720
and it's absolutely heartbreaking for me,

638
00:35:33,190 --> 00:35:34,560
so please just cancel it.

639
00:35:36,060 --> 00:35:37,900
Okay. Then as of today,

640
00:35:37,960 --> 00:35:40,270
I will process the cancellation for you.

641
00:35:45,800 --> 00:35:47,770
Excuse me...

642
00:35:48,710 --> 00:35:51,310
I graduated from a prestigious medical school in Korea,

643
00:35:51,480 --> 00:35:53,440
then immediately from a famous medical school in the US,

644
00:35:53,510 --> 00:35:54,580
and I'm working as a salaried doctor...

645
00:35:54,580 --> 00:35:56,010
at a dermatology clinic in Apgujeong.

646
00:35:56,380 --> 00:35:58,520
By any chance,

647
00:35:58,720 --> 00:36:01,350
what's the maximum for a line of credit?

648
00:36:02,690 --> 00:36:03,890
One moment, please.

649
00:36:10,090 --> 00:36:15,100
(Daebak Loan Capital)

650
00:36:17,370 --> 00:36:19,200
(Daebak Loan Capital)

651
00:36:27,050 --> 00:36:29,050
(Quick Cash Specialist No-Collateral Daily and Monthly Loans)

652
00:36:59,810 --> 00:37:01,150
Darn it...

653
00:37:10,890 --> 00:37:12,320
(Same-Day Loans, Major Discounts Daebak Loan Capital)

654
00:37:12,620 --> 00:37:13,630
No.

655
00:37:14,190 --> 00:37:17,260
Once I'm married, I can pay it back in no time.

656
00:37:18,600 --> 00:37:20,370
My future husband's family is a conglomerate.

657
00:37:21,270 --> 00:37:22,330
A conglomerate.

658
00:37:33,880 --> 00:37:37,780
Stop walking on eggshells around me, and just say what you need to say.

659
00:37:38,480 --> 00:37:41,520
What could I possibly say?

660
00:37:41,950 --> 00:37:43,350
If I could find a mouse hole to crawl into,

661
00:37:43,420 --> 00:37:46,560
I'd want to just go and hide.

662
00:37:47,890 --> 00:37:50,160
We can't have a mouse hole in a side dish shop.

663
00:37:50,530 --> 00:37:52,000
We'd have to close down then.

664
00:37:53,900 --> 00:37:55,930
Oh my, you're smiling at me.

665
00:37:56,900 --> 00:37:58,800
Does that mean you've already forgiven me?

666
00:38:00,810 --> 00:38:03,610
If I were in your shoes, Ma'am, I would've done the same thing.

667
00:38:04,780 --> 00:38:06,440
You had every right to be angry.

668
00:38:06,540 --> 00:38:07,550
Oh, dear.

669
00:38:07,980 --> 00:38:11,050
Hey now, stop trying to be so understanding...

670
00:38:11,120 --> 00:38:13,120
and just curse me out instead, okay?

671
00:38:13,120 --> 00:38:15,550
Say, "You darned old hag."

672
00:38:15,720 --> 00:38:17,260
Or, "You should've listened and believed me..."

673
00:38:17,320 --> 00:38:18,320
"in the first place."

674
00:38:18,390 --> 00:38:20,360
"Are you old and stupid or something?"

675
00:38:22,890 --> 00:38:24,260
I'll do better.

676
00:38:25,300 --> 00:38:26,430
I want you to be able to say,

677
00:38:26,430 --> 00:38:28,800
"I'd believe Gyu Rim even if she told me pigs could fly."

678
00:38:28,900 --> 00:38:31,600
I'll do so much better that you'll say that about me.

679
00:38:32,140 --> 00:38:33,140
Goodness.

680
00:38:33,810 --> 00:38:38,440
Honestly. You're a saint.

681
00:38:39,310 --> 00:38:42,350
So how could I not fall for you?

682
00:38:45,880 --> 00:38:48,720
Hey, it's past lunchtime.

683
00:38:48,890 --> 00:38:50,220
Let's pull down the shutter for a bit...

684
00:38:50,290 --> 00:38:52,890
and go get some ribs at the place up front, shall we?

685
00:38:54,530 --> 00:38:56,560
Let's eat together when Heung Sik gets better.

686
00:38:56,830 --> 00:38:58,000
Oh my.

687
00:38:58,060 --> 00:39:01,600
You're already looking out for our Heung Sik like this?

688
00:39:03,070 --> 00:39:07,040
I'd better not tell that boy. He'd be so touched.

689
00:39:07,410 --> 00:39:09,540
What if he has a heart attack and dies on the spot?

690
00:39:09,540 --> 00:39:10,780
No, no. That just won't do.

691
00:39:12,580 --> 00:39:14,650
- I should stir-fry the vegetables. - Okay, you do that.

692
00:39:19,880 --> 00:39:23,420
You know? I'm having a hard time keeping my mouth shut.

693
00:39:23,860 --> 00:39:25,490
I feel like grabbing a bullhorn...

694
00:39:25,560 --> 00:39:28,490
and announcing that Han Gyu Rim and Jo Heung Sik are dating.

695
00:39:28,690 --> 00:39:30,730
I'm going to spread that rumour, you hear?

696
00:39:32,460 --> 00:39:34,330
He hasn't given me an answer yet.

697
00:39:34,500 --> 00:39:37,570
What? He still hasn't answered you?

698
00:39:38,570 --> 00:39:39,800
He has nothing to do.

699
00:39:39,870 --> 00:39:42,140
Why is he dragging his feet?

700
00:39:44,310 --> 00:39:46,310
He probably needs time to think.

701
00:39:46,980 --> 00:39:48,710
Think? What's there to think about?

702
00:39:49,010 --> 00:39:52,320
He's just hit a once-in-a-lifetime jackpot,

703
00:39:52,550 --> 00:39:55,120
and he's completely lost his mind, that boy, hasn't he?

704
00:39:55,550 --> 00:39:59,120
He doesn't know how good he has it. That rotten kid.

705
00:40:03,430 --> 00:40:05,930
Oh, this is just great, isn't it?

706
00:40:18,940 --> 00:40:19,940
You know who I am, right?

707
00:40:21,150 --> 00:40:22,410
No, I don't.

708
00:40:23,680 --> 00:40:24,680
You really don't?

709
00:40:25,280 --> 00:40:27,650
I said I don't know you. Who are you?

710
00:40:28,790 --> 00:40:31,160
Good job. Good job, Kwon Hee Na.

711
00:40:32,160 --> 00:40:33,790
What good would it do to say I know him?

712
00:40:34,360 --> 00:40:35,360
You did the right thing.

713
00:40:36,130 --> 00:40:37,130
Yes.

714
00:40:37,200 --> 00:40:38,660
(Mrs. Park Su Nam)

715
00:40:43,100 --> 00:40:45,670
- Yes, Ma'am. - Is this a good time?

716
00:40:45,670 --> 00:40:47,540
I hope I'm not bothering you.

717
00:40:47,610 --> 00:40:48,610
No, it's fine.

718
00:40:48,910 --> 00:40:51,180
I made some side dishes that you like.

719
00:40:51,280 --> 00:40:53,280
Come and get them. No, no, on second thought.

720
00:40:53,380 --> 00:40:56,680
If you don't have any plans, just come to my place for dinner.

721
00:40:57,080 --> 00:40:59,820
If Heung Sik were alright, I'd have him bring them to you.

722
00:41:00,180 --> 00:41:01,590
What's wrong with Heung Sik?

723
00:41:02,390 --> 00:41:06,420
It's nothing serious. He just got a little hurt.

724
00:41:06,960 --> 00:41:08,830
I see.

725
00:41:09,660 --> 00:41:12,030
I'll go visit him after work tonight.

726
00:41:12,360 --> 00:41:14,800
(Kwon Hee Na)

727
00:41:16,970 --> 00:41:18,770
You're going to stare a hole through your phone.

728
00:41:19,700 --> 00:41:21,440
Are you waiting for a call or something?

729
00:41:23,140 --> 00:41:26,010
I left a voice message, but I think I'm being ignored.

730
00:41:26,940 --> 00:41:28,680
There's a girl ignoring you?

731
00:41:29,580 --> 00:41:31,980
Oh, right. Thanks for helping me with this suit.

732
00:41:32,050 --> 00:41:33,050
Everything went well.

733
00:41:33,580 --> 00:41:35,250
Where did you go?

734
00:41:35,520 --> 00:41:37,150
You don't need to know.

735
00:41:39,890 --> 00:41:42,860
And I heard someone is coming to visit me tonight.

736
00:41:43,390 --> 00:41:45,200
She's a nice girl your age,

737
00:41:45,260 --> 00:41:46,730
so you two could be friends or something.

738
00:41:47,500 --> 00:41:49,430
I'm not friends with women.

739
00:41:50,270 --> 00:41:51,270
Oh, come on.

740
00:41:52,200 --> 00:41:53,700
Help me get this off.

741
00:41:55,410 --> 00:41:57,610
- I can't do it alone. - Oh, honestly.

742
00:41:58,140 --> 00:42:00,080
- Sorry. - Take your arm out.

743
00:42:00,140 --> 00:42:03,010
- Gosh. - Okay, let's get this off.

744
00:42:08,290 --> 00:42:10,320
- Thank you. - You're welcome.

745
00:42:12,560 --> 00:42:15,860
I should buy some fruit that he likes.

746
00:42:23,470 --> 00:42:26,940
Okay, over there. Yes, that's it. That's it.

747
00:42:27,270 --> 00:42:29,340
Right? This one goes over there.

748
00:42:29,840 --> 00:42:30,840
That's it.

749
00:42:32,810 --> 00:42:35,850
- Mustard leaf kimchi. - There's more?

750
00:42:35,910 --> 00:42:36,910
Gosh.

751
00:42:45,460 --> 00:42:47,090
(Kim Yoon Gi)

752
00:42:50,760 --> 00:42:51,760
What?

753
00:42:51,830 --> 00:42:53,530
Gyu Oh, is the girl you're looking for Kwon Hee Na?

754
00:42:54,830 --> 00:42:55,830
So what if she is?

755
00:42:58,440 --> 00:42:59,440
Where are you now?

756
00:43:01,610 --> 00:43:02,770
Okay, I know where it is. I'll be right there.

757
00:44:03,300 --> 00:44:04,500
Gyu Oh, over here.

758
00:44:09,540 --> 00:44:10,980
This is my friend Han Gyu Oh,

759
00:44:11,910 --> 00:44:14,010
and this is my girlfriend, Suh Min Ju.

760
00:44:14,010 --> 00:44:16,310
- Hello. - Nice to meet you.

761
00:44:17,920 --> 00:44:20,020
We were just talking, and Kwon Hee Na's name came up.

762
00:44:20,420 --> 00:44:22,320
Min Ju said she thinks it's someone she knows.

763
00:44:26,120 --> 00:44:28,790
Gosh, this Kwon Hee Na must be really something.

764
00:44:29,590 --> 00:44:30,900
I mean, usually when I call you,

765
00:44:30,960 --> 00:44:32,300
you're too busy or can't be bothered,

766
00:44:32,930 --> 00:44:33,930
and you're the one who never budges.

767
00:44:34,170 --> 00:44:35,170
You know Kwon Hee Na?

768
00:44:36,170 --> 00:44:37,170
Well...

769
00:44:37,570 --> 00:44:39,200
At least catch your breath, man.

770
00:44:39,340 --> 00:44:41,410
Could you possibly show me a picture?

771
00:44:41,740 --> 00:44:42,740
Gyu Oh.

772
00:44:50,510 --> 00:44:52,280
This isn't something weird, is it?

773
00:44:53,250 --> 00:44:54,250
Of course not, honey.

774
00:44:54,590 --> 00:44:56,450
She's a girl that Gyu Oh was really in love with,

775
00:44:56,550 --> 00:44:58,490
and he just wants to confirm if it's her or not.

776
00:44:59,260 --> 00:45:00,830
He won't be a bother at all,

777
00:45:01,090 --> 00:45:02,660
and he won't put you in an awkward position.

778
00:45:03,060 --> 00:45:04,730
Come on, don't you trust me?

779
00:45:37,730 --> 00:45:38,730
Goodness.

780
00:45:38,800 --> 00:45:39,900
Honestly.

781
00:45:40,360 --> 00:45:42,730
I'm nearly 70 years old,

782
00:45:42,900 --> 00:45:46,370
and who knew I'd still be feeding my 40-year-old son?

783
00:45:46,640 --> 00:45:48,010
Weren't you just saying I was doing great?

784
00:45:49,540 --> 00:45:50,710
Yes, I was.

785
00:45:51,380 --> 00:45:54,380
That's right. You did do a good job, yes.

786
00:45:55,110 --> 00:45:58,850
And thanks to that, Gyu Rim even asked you out.

787
00:45:59,080 --> 00:46:00,080
What?

788
00:46:00,750 --> 00:46:03,250
What? Heung Sik, someone asked you out?

789
00:46:04,120 --> 00:46:05,220
No.

790
00:46:05,290 --> 00:46:06,920
What do you mean, no?

791
00:46:08,160 --> 00:46:10,800
Hey, he's just saying that because he's embarrassed.

792
00:46:11,800 --> 00:46:12,800
Oh, right.

793
00:46:12,860 --> 00:46:15,630
Hee Na, didn't you get a phone call?

794
00:46:15,700 --> 00:46:16,970
Pardon? What call?

795
00:46:17,270 --> 00:46:20,100
Well, from the younger brother of the woman...

796
00:46:20,100 --> 00:46:21,240
who asked Heung Sik out.

797
00:46:21,710 --> 00:46:24,910
He was just here helping set the table a moment ago.

798
00:46:25,280 --> 00:46:26,380
Anyway,

799
00:46:26,710 --> 00:46:30,380
if all goes well, he could become our in-law.

800
00:46:30,450 --> 00:46:33,320
Oh, honestly, who are you trying to matchmake now?

801
00:46:33,520 --> 00:46:35,350
It's not like I would give...

802
00:46:35,420 --> 00:46:38,990
your number to just anybody, Hee Na.

803
00:46:40,020 --> 00:46:43,530
The woman at the rice cake shop said he looks like a pretty boy.

804
00:46:43,930 --> 00:46:46,000
Anyway, he's not what he looks like.

805
00:46:46,530 --> 00:46:50,770
He's very thoughtful, kind, and hardworking, you know?

806
00:46:51,240 --> 00:46:53,470
Honestly, right after my Heung Sik,

807
00:46:53,540 --> 00:46:55,340
he's the man whose character I can vouch for the most.

808
00:46:56,070 --> 00:46:58,080
I'm not interested in dating anyone right now.

809
00:46:58,210 --> 00:47:00,850
No, that's not what I meant...

810
00:47:00,910 --> 00:47:04,220
Gosh, have you gotten hooked on matchmaking or something?

811
00:47:04,450 --> 00:47:06,820
Kids these days can handle that on their own.

812
00:47:06,880 --> 00:47:08,990
You need to learn to read the room.

813
00:47:09,520 --> 00:47:11,590
Read the room? What's that?

814
00:47:11,660 --> 00:47:13,620
Know when to butt in and when to butt out.

815
00:47:13,690 --> 00:47:15,330
You're so clueless, Mother.

816
00:47:15,390 --> 00:47:17,190
When I feel like I want to date someone,

817
00:47:17,260 --> 00:47:18,900
I promise I'll let you know then,

818
00:47:18,960 --> 00:47:20,660
so please, you can be the one to introduce me to someone.

819
00:47:20,730 --> 00:47:24,030
No, no, that's not what I meant.

820
00:47:24,100 --> 00:47:27,100
Didn't you hear Hee Na say she's not interested?

821
00:47:27,170 --> 00:47:29,840
Just give me more rice. With some of that dried radish.

822
00:47:30,340 --> 00:47:31,410
Am I your servant?

823
00:47:32,440 --> 00:47:36,810
And besides, why aren't you giving Gyu Rim an answer?

824
00:47:37,410 --> 00:47:39,520
Who do you think you are? Do you think you're all that?

825
00:47:39,580 --> 00:47:40,990
Do you think it's because I think I'm all that?

826
00:47:41,690 --> 00:47:43,290
It's because I'm not good enough.

827
00:47:43,520 --> 00:47:44,960
What's not good enough about you?

828
00:47:45,190 --> 00:47:46,420
After everything I did to raise you?

829
00:47:46,490 --> 00:47:50,060
- What's not good enough about you? - Please, stop twisting my words.

830
00:47:50,130 --> 00:47:51,730
When did I twist your words?

831
00:47:51,800 --> 00:47:53,000
I haven't twisted a thing, you brat.

832
00:47:53,060 --> 00:47:55,970
Grandma, Uncle, will you two please stop?

833
00:47:56,030 --> 00:47:57,370
Let's just eat, please.

834
00:47:57,740 --> 00:47:59,000
Right. Let's just eat.

835
00:47:59,070 --> 00:48:01,310
If you keep this up, I'm really going home.

836
00:48:01,670 --> 00:48:03,940
You worthless brat.

837
00:48:04,010 --> 00:48:05,040
Hey, just eat...

838
00:48:12,480 --> 00:48:13,980
She's the one who asked to meet,

839
00:48:13,980 --> 00:48:15,820
so what right does she have to keep us waiting?

840
00:48:16,220 --> 00:48:17,220
I know.

841
00:48:17,420 --> 00:48:18,690
I guess her meeting ran a little long.

842
00:48:19,060 --> 00:48:20,320
She said she'd be here soon.

843
00:48:22,790 --> 00:48:23,790
Honestly,

844
00:48:24,530 --> 00:48:26,460
I can't stand the mom or the son.

845
00:48:34,310 --> 00:48:35,440
Mr. Kim. Yes.

846
00:48:35,910 --> 00:48:38,310
Can I call you back in about two hours?

847
00:48:39,410 --> 00:48:40,410
Pardon?

848
00:48:41,950 --> 00:48:43,850
I'm telling you, you can't do that.

849
00:48:44,980 --> 00:48:46,850
I'm going to step out and take this call.

850
00:48:47,620 --> 00:48:49,420
No, I told Director Park to send you an email.

851
00:48:49,420 --> 00:48:50,420
Didn't you get it?

852
00:48:51,260 --> 00:48:52,260
Yes.

853
00:49:07,640 --> 00:49:10,510
Goodness. Where are you going? Are you going to the restroom?

854
00:49:12,010 --> 00:49:13,010
No.

855
00:49:13,710 --> 00:49:14,880
I'm going home.

856
00:49:17,210 --> 00:49:18,550
Where did Hoon Tae go?

857
00:49:19,780 --> 00:49:21,490
He went to take a call.

858
00:49:22,150 --> 00:49:23,450
When he comes back,

859
00:49:23,690 --> 00:49:25,160
you two can have your meal.

860
00:49:25,820 --> 00:49:28,290
Wait. But...

861
00:49:29,160 --> 00:49:31,460
why are you so upset?

862
00:49:33,330 --> 00:49:36,270
Is it because I was a little late?

863
00:49:37,230 --> 00:49:40,770
Come on. I was only 40 minutes late.

864
00:49:42,010 --> 00:49:43,510
Only 40 minutes?

865
00:49:44,980 --> 00:49:48,880
We're not usually this prickly with each other.

866
00:49:49,010 --> 00:49:50,410
More than anyone,

867
00:49:50,710 --> 00:49:54,390
you've always understood and overlooked my flaws.

868
00:49:54,950 --> 00:49:58,620
And if things go well, we'll become in-laws.

869
00:49:59,720 --> 00:50:00,720
Who will?

870
00:50:01,490 --> 00:50:03,030
You and my family, Chairman?

871
00:50:03,630 --> 00:50:04,760
Says who?

872
00:50:06,130 --> 00:50:07,130
Yoon Hee.

873
00:50:07,200 --> 00:50:10,570
I don't have the slightest desire to have Mu Jin as a son-in-law.

874
00:50:11,500 --> 00:50:13,800
That's why I came here today.

875
00:50:15,210 --> 00:50:17,070
What should I do?

876
00:50:17,410 --> 00:50:19,210
What can I do to make you feel a little better...

877
00:50:19,280 --> 00:50:20,480
Don't do anything.

878
00:50:21,150 --> 00:50:24,310
Nothing you do will change my mind.

879
00:50:36,090 --> 00:50:37,330
That girl from back then.

880
00:50:38,300 --> 00:50:39,830
The one Mu Jin supposedly liked.

881
00:50:40,630 --> 00:50:42,330
From that dirt-poor family,

882
00:50:42,830 --> 00:50:43,830
with a widowed father,

883
00:50:44,370 --> 00:50:46,300
a line of younger siblings, and just a high school diploma.

884
00:50:48,210 --> 00:50:50,340
Oh, is this all because of her?

885
00:50:51,510 --> 00:50:52,510
And here I was thinking...

886
00:50:53,080 --> 00:50:56,310
No, he broke up with her long ago.

887
00:50:56,380 --> 00:50:59,150
Eight years ago. It was a clean break.

888
00:51:01,090 --> 00:51:02,820
Are you sure they really broke up?

889
00:51:03,150 --> 00:51:04,150
Oh, for goodness' sake.

890
00:51:04,720 --> 00:51:06,960
I mean, Mu Jin and I forgot about her long ago,

891
00:51:07,060 --> 00:51:10,160
but you still remembered, Yoon Hee? Goodness.

892
00:51:10,860 --> 00:51:14,330
I'm telling you, she was just a gold digger.

893
00:51:15,300 --> 00:51:17,800
How would you know if she's a gold digger or not, Chairman?

894
00:51:18,700 --> 00:51:21,240
Did you see her acting like one, Chairman?

895
00:51:21,910 --> 00:51:22,910
Yoon Hee.

896
00:51:22,970 --> 00:51:25,810
To her parents, that child must be precious and cherished too.

897
00:51:26,710 --> 00:51:29,080
How can you be so reckless with your words?

898
00:51:29,910 --> 00:51:32,550
If her parents heard you, it would break their hearts.

899
00:51:33,220 --> 00:51:34,220
Listen here.

900
00:51:34,380 --> 00:51:36,190
For someone who's supposed to be the Chairman of a company,

901
00:51:36,820 --> 00:51:38,620
is this all the decency you have?

902
00:51:41,990 --> 00:51:43,190
Yoon Hee,

903
00:51:43,890 --> 00:51:47,430
I think you're crossing a line with me.

904
00:51:47,900 --> 00:51:48,900
Right?

905
00:51:50,800 --> 00:51:52,870
You're the one who has crossed the line, Chairman.

906
00:51:54,510 --> 00:51:55,540
Anyway, I...

907
00:51:56,340 --> 00:51:58,010
will never, ever...

908
00:51:58,710 --> 00:52:00,410
approve of them dating.

909
00:52:10,690 --> 00:52:13,920
Oh, honestly. My goodness, this is ridiculous.

910
00:52:17,060 --> 00:52:18,300
Calm down.

911
00:52:19,000 --> 00:52:21,730
Patience can prevent a murder. Calm down, now.

912
00:52:23,530 --> 00:52:24,540
You're here?

913
00:52:26,340 --> 00:52:28,170
Did my wife go to the restroom?

914
00:52:28,370 --> 00:52:29,610
Where have you been?

915
00:52:30,310 --> 00:52:31,940
Your wife went home.

916
00:52:32,710 --> 00:52:33,710
What?

917
00:52:34,440 --> 00:52:37,710
- Really? - That's it. I've had it.

918
00:52:37,780 --> 00:52:41,290
- Why is your wife being dramatic? - About what?

919
00:52:41,350 --> 00:52:42,590
Honestly, anyone would think...

920
00:52:42,820 --> 00:52:45,890
she was that gold digger's mother.

921
00:52:46,160 --> 00:52:47,520
What are you talking about now?

922
00:52:48,690 --> 00:52:49,690
Hold on.

923
00:52:50,530 --> 00:52:52,000
Oh, honestly.

924
00:52:55,500 --> 00:52:56,800
Is this really your best?

925
00:52:57,300 --> 00:52:59,870
Do you really think this face resembles this one?

926
00:53:01,870 --> 00:53:04,270
You may not be satisfied right now,

927
00:53:04,640 --> 00:53:06,640
but there's still time before the wedding.

928
00:53:07,210 --> 00:53:10,650
With a proper diet and exercise, we'll get him as slim as possible.

929
00:53:10,850 --> 00:53:13,180
And with some skillful cover-up makeup,

930
00:53:13,480 --> 00:53:15,990
it'll be a 100 percent, no, 120 percent match.

931
00:53:16,720 --> 00:53:20,090
Here, take a look. If you look here, Look.

932
00:53:20,590 --> 00:53:23,090
This face transforms into this one.

933
00:53:23,390 --> 00:53:25,160
Before and after.

934
00:53:25,600 --> 00:53:26,860
Perfect.

935
00:53:28,330 --> 00:53:29,870
- Just a moment. - Of course.

936
00:53:31,340 --> 00:53:32,340
Yes, Dad.

937
00:53:32,670 --> 00:53:34,540
What should I wear to your wedding?

938
00:53:35,140 --> 00:53:36,370
Anything.

939
00:53:36,970 --> 00:53:38,580
You have such great features...

940
00:53:38,640 --> 00:53:41,710
- that you look good in anything. - I should get some skincare too.

941
00:53:42,080 --> 00:53:43,210
Should I go to your clinic?

942
00:53:44,110 --> 00:53:46,820
Why would someone with perfect skin like you need that?

943
00:53:47,080 --> 00:53:49,220
Dad, I'm really busy right now.

944
00:53:49,420 --> 00:53:50,920
I'll call you back in a little while.

945
00:53:52,760 --> 00:53:53,760
Darn it.

946
00:53:58,830 --> 00:54:00,930
So, shall we get back to it?

947
00:54:02,230 --> 00:54:04,570
- Yes. - There's just one problem.

948
00:54:05,600 --> 00:54:06,600
A problem?

949
00:54:06,700 --> 00:54:08,040
This person...

950
00:54:08,940 --> 00:54:09,940
is...

951
00:54:11,140 --> 00:54:12,410
only 150cm tall.

952
00:54:13,110 --> 00:54:15,280
Of course, we'll have him wear elevator shoes.

953
00:54:15,280 --> 00:54:16,450
What?

954
00:54:16,850 --> 00:54:19,280
How can you tell me something this important just now?

955
00:54:21,690 --> 00:54:24,690
We can say he had a major accident right before the wedding,

956
00:54:25,020 --> 00:54:26,460
and put him in a wheelchair...

957
00:54:26,560 --> 00:54:28,860
You're a complete con artist, aren't you?

958
00:54:29,330 --> 00:54:31,460
And you have the audacity to ask for 10,000 dollars for this?

959
00:54:31,700 --> 00:54:32,960
Do you take me for a fool?

960
00:54:33,530 --> 00:54:35,970
Who are you calling a con artist?

961
00:54:36,500 --> 00:54:37,930
Who proposed this con in the first place?

962
00:54:38,770 --> 00:54:40,800
- What? - I went out of my way...

963
00:54:40,800 --> 00:54:42,470
because you're my niece's acquaintance,

964
00:54:42,540 --> 00:54:44,310
found actors who fit your criteria,

965
00:54:44,440 --> 00:54:46,210
and even came up with a contingency plan.

966
00:54:46,880 --> 00:54:48,010
And you have the nerve to...

967
00:54:48,880 --> 00:54:52,620
Forget it. Forget it. I'm not doing it.

968
00:54:53,150 --> 00:54:55,520
I don't have to. This is too sleazy for me to do.

969
00:54:58,490 --> 00:55:00,990
Darn it. Wait a minute.

970
00:55:01,330 --> 00:55:02,930
Wait.

971
00:55:05,160 --> 00:55:06,360
I'm sorry.

972
00:55:06,430 --> 00:55:08,070
I was just caught off guard, and I overreacted.

973
00:55:08,400 --> 00:55:09,970
Instead of putting him in a wheelchair,

974
00:55:10,030 --> 00:55:11,300
let's say he's seriously injured.

975
00:55:11,500 --> 00:55:13,300
We could wrap his face in bandages...

976
00:55:13,800 --> 00:55:15,340
and have him lie in a bed. How about that?

977
00:55:23,080 --> 00:55:24,250
We're closed for the day.

978
00:55:24,450 --> 00:55:26,420
I'm here about the part-time job posting.

979
00:55:26,950 --> 00:55:27,950
By any chance,

980
00:55:28,020 --> 00:55:29,350
have you already filled the position?

981
00:55:30,850 --> 00:55:32,160
Someone's here about the job ad.

982
00:55:34,190 --> 00:55:35,190
A student?

983
00:55:35,260 --> 00:55:36,490
Yes, I'm a junior in high school.

984
00:55:36,830 --> 00:55:38,600
Did you bring your resume and health certificate?

985
00:55:39,260 --> 00:55:40,260
Yes.

986
00:55:41,400 --> 00:55:42,400
Okay.

987
00:55:47,940 --> 00:55:50,570
You have a lot of experience at other restaurants.

988
00:55:50,640 --> 00:55:51,710
Is this your dream career path?

989
00:55:52,040 --> 00:55:55,210
No. My dream is to be a designer.

990
00:55:55,980 --> 00:55:57,850
But I'll do a great job at anything you give me.

991
00:55:59,980 --> 00:56:02,450
Seeing as you brought your health certificate in advance,

992
00:56:02,520 --> 00:56:04,920
you must have checked the hourly wage...

993
00:56:04,990 --> 00:56:07,120
and other conditions on the site.

994
00:56:07,190 --> 00:56:09,830
- Yes. - What?

995
00:56:11,560 --> 00:56:13,800
Oh, nothing. I was just thinking out loud.

996
00:56:17,500 --> 00:56:20,940
But I like your quick response. All right then,

997
00:56:21,810 --> 00:56:23,240
you can start tomorrow.

998
00:56:23,840 --> 00:56:26,940
For now, you'll work weekdays from dinner service to closing.

999
00:56:27,010 --> 00:56:29,580
And weekends from opening through lunch service.

1000
00:56:30,280 --> 00:56:32,680
What? Did I get the job?

1001
00:56:33,050 --> 00:56:34,280
You're not going to ask me anything else?

1002
00:56:34,380 --> 00:56:35,420
That's right.

1003
00:56:35,420 --> 00:56:38,260
We were looking for someone sharp and efficient,

1004
00:56:38,320 --> 00:56:40,020
and as it turns out, someone like you showed up.

1005
00:56:40,660 --> 00:56:41,660
So I'd say you got the job.

1006
00:56:42,330 --> 00:56:43,590
Yes, I think so.

1007
00:56:44,690 --> 00:56:46,960
I'll see you tomorrow, then. I'll work hard.

1008
00:56:58,310 --> 00:57:01,810
She's perfect. But of all people, why Han Gyu Min?

1009
00:57:02,510 --> 00:57:03,510
Han Gyu Rim.

1010
00:57:04,820 --> 00:57:07,720
Just when I thought I was getting away from Han Gyeol...

1011
00:57:09,790 --> 00:57:11,390
I mean, it's not like in all of Korea,

1012
00:57:11,490 --> 00:57:13,620
there's only one family with the last name Han.

1013
00:57:13,960 --> 00:57:15,230
I'm getting carried away.

1014
00:57:16,160 --> 00:57:17,360
Way too carried away.

1015
00:57:19,730 --> 00:57:21,300
Yes, that's good.

1016
00:57:22,000 --> 00:57:24,800
Okay. Just like that.

1017
00:57:24,940 --> 00:57:26,200
Yes, that's great.

1018
00:57:26,270 --> 00:57:29,370
- Okay, let's take a short break. - Okay.

1019
00:57:37,280 --> 00:57:39,120
- Hello, Ms. Kim. - Hi.

1020
00:57:43,290 --> 00:57:46,060
- Are these the new models? - Yes, that's right.

1021
00:57:46,160 --> 00:57:47,920
I don't think I've seen the male model before.

1022
00:57:48,730 --> 00:57:50,290
- Is he new? - Yes.

1023
00:57:50,790 --> 00:57:54,500
He's a sophomore in high school, and since he just started modelling,

1024
00:57:55,000 --> 00:57:56,700
he doesn't have much experience with shows or photo shoots.

1025
00:57:57,030 --> 00:58:01,570
But in the final round of auditions, he was the unanimous choice.

1026
00:58:02,910 --> 00:58:04,270
Okay, let's get back to it.

1027
00:58:07,180 --> 00:58:08,180
Good.

1028
00:58:08,410 --> 00:58:09,880
- Nice. - Yes.

1029
00:58:13,750 --> 00:58:14,920
He's a good pick.

1030
00:58:14,920 --> 00:58:17,390
- Not sure he'll be a star, but... - Good.

1031
00:58:17,820 --> 00:58:19,490
at least he won't be a flop.

1032
00:58:23,490 --> 00:58:24,730
Yes, you look great.

1033
00:58:26,360 --> 00:58:27,930
Okay, in for a close-up.

1034
00:58:38,540 --> 00:58:40,610
I'm fine. I'm not cold.

1035
00:58:42,550 --> 00:58:43,550
Just put it on.

1036
00:58:44,110 --> 00:58:45,580
It gets pretty chilly at night.

1037
00:58:57,290 --> 00:58:58,460
What time do you get discharged tomorrow?

1038
00:58:59,430 --> 00:59:00,600
Around 3 or 4 in the afternoon?

1039
00:59:00,960 --> 00:59:01,970
Okay.

1040
00:59:02,970 --> 00:59:04,100
I'll come pick you up.

1041
00:59:04,430 --> 00:59:06,700
Tell your parents I'm coming to get you.

1042
00:59:08,370 --> 00:59:09,770
No, don't come.

1043
00:59:10,570 --> 00:59:12,380
You'll just run into my mom again.

1044
00:59:13,280 --> 00:59:17,280
For now, it's best if you and my mom don't run into each other.

1045
00:59:19,350 --> 00:59:20,550
Okay, I understand.

1046
00:59:22,250 --> 00:59:24,750
No matter what my mom says, don't give up on me.

1047
00:59:27,460 --> 00:59:30,290
Gyu Rim. No matter what happens,

1048
00:59:31,130 --> 00:59:32,300
don't give up on me.

1049
00:59:38,370 --> 00:59:39,400
What is it?

1050
00:59:39,400 --> 00:59:42,510
I'm just so happy that I can't believe it.

1051
00:59:44,840 --> 00:59:46,010
Your button's undone.

1052
00:59:50,910 --> 00:59:52,250
He's my boyfriend.

1053
00:59:53,220 --> 00:59:55,420
This man is my boyfriend.

1054
00:59:55,620 --> 00:59:58,320
- Seo Hyun. - This man is my boyfriend!

1055
01:00:00,290 --> 01:00:03,030
This man is mine. He's my boyfriend.

1056
01:00:06,460 --> 01:00:07,600
What is it?

1057
01:00:31,860 --> 01:00:32,960
Thank you.

1058
01:00:44,970 --> 01:00:46,140
What is all this?

1059
01:00:47,740 --> 01:00:49,070
What do you think? They're gifts for my future in-laws.

1060
01:00:49,140 --> 01:00:50,370
You could at least offer to help if you noticed.

1061
01:00:51,210 --> 01:00:53,080
Actually, no. You'll just get the bags dirty.

1062
01:00:53,140 --> 01:00:55,910
- Don't touch them. - Where'd you get money for this?

1063
01:00:56,950 --> 01:00:58,250
Isn't all this incredibly expensive?

1064
01:01:00,020 --> 01:01:02,090
It's not stolen money, so don't worry.

1065
01:01:04,550 --> 01:01:05,690
Let's get a drink.

1066
01:01:08,260 --> 01:01:09,590
My wedding is in three weeks.

1067
01:01:09,690 --> 01:01:11,930
You think I want to get my dress refitted?

1068
01:01:12,200 --> 01:01:14,260
Fine, you don't have to drink. I'll drink alone.

1069
01:01:16,970 --> 01:01:19,500
I have something extremely important to talk about.

1070
01:01:19,840 --> 01:01:21,170
Don't even think about running off, and follow me.

1071
01:01:24,140 --> 01:01:25,540
Why is she being so dramatic?

1072
01:01:28,240 --> 01:01:30,380
You can't even drink. What's this about getting a drink?

1073
01:01:31,280 --> 01:01:32,380
Darn it.

1074
01:01:57,570 --> 01:02:00,310
Darn it. I'm an idiot for falling for this.

1075
01:02:00,710 --> 01:02:02,210
I'm sorry, Gyu Young.

1076
01:02:05,010 --> 01:02:06,580
My little sister is getting married,

1077
01:02:07,380 --> 01:02:08,890
and as her older sister,

1078
01:02:09,690 --> 01:02:11,190
I haven't been able to help at all.

1079
01:02:13,820 --> 01:02:15,160
I'm truly sorry.

1080
01:02:16,960 --> 01:02:18,030
Well, as long as you know.

1081
01:02:18,530 --> 01:02:20,800
Is that why you called me here?

1082
01:02:21,660 --> 01:02:22,900
This is so annoying, darn it.

1083
01:02:23,300 --> 01:02:24,900
But since I already feel bad,

1084
01:02:26,900 --> 01:02:28,300
I might as well go all the way.

1085
01:02:29,140 --> 01:02:30,140
What?

1086
01:02:30,670 --> 01:02:31,740
I have to...

1087
01:02:32,380 --> 01:02:34,840
- stop your marriage. - Hey!

1088
01:02:34,840 --> 01:02:36,580
The lies you told your future husband's family...

1089
01:02:38,010 --> 01:02:39,580
You need to come clean about everything...

1090
01:02:40,020 --> 01:02:42,220
- by tomorrow. - Are you crazy?

1091
01:02:42,390 --> 01:02:43,650
If you don't go, I will.

1092
01:02:45,490 --> 01:02:47,890
And how would you know where to go? How would you know who they are?

1093
01:02:50,230 --> 01:02:51,560
I'm sure Heung Sik knows.

1094
01:02:56,630 --> 01:02:58,970
You know that when I snap, I really snap, right?

1095
01:03:00,170 --> 01:03:01,970
And that when I do, no one can stop me.

1096
01:03:02,870 --> 01:03:03,910
You know that, don't you?

1097
01:03:04,810 --> 01:03:07,840
Hey, seriously... You're my sister.

1098
01:03:08,280 --> 01:03:10,780
No matter how embarrassing our family is,

1099
01:03:11,510 --> 01:03:14,580
how could you hire our father as a part-timer?

1100
01:03:16,550 --> 01:03:17,550
No.

1101
01:03:18,660 --> 01:03:19,960
It was my fault.

1102
01:03:21,160 --> 01:03:23,290
I should have stopped you back then.

1103
01:03:24,360 --> 01:03:25,430
He's not a part-timer.

1104
01:03:26,630 --> 01:03:28,260
He's a father too.

1105
01:03:29,230 --> 01:03:30,900
If he's Mom's husband, that makes him a father, right?

1106
01:03:33,200 --> 01:03:34,270
What are you talking about?

1107
01:03:37,710 --> 01:03:39,610
He's the man Mom remarried.

1108
01:03:40,610 --> 01:03:42,710
Between Mom's ex-husband and her current husband,

1109
01:03:42,710 --> 01:03:45,250
I chose the better father.

1110
01:03:48,080 --> 01:03:49,290
I didn't lie about anything.

1111
01:03:50,950 --> 01:03:52,490
You're so infuriating.

1112
01:05:14,800 --> 01:05:16,770
(Love on the Menu)

1113
01:05:17,010 --> 01:05:19,780
Excuse me, was anything turned in to the lost and found yesterday?

1114
01:05:19,980 --> 01:05:21,180
What did you lose?

1115
01:05:21,280 --> 01:05:25,720
I'm sure I lost something, but I don't know what it was.

1116
01:05:25,820 --> 01:05:27,250
Who? Han Gyu Oh?

1117
01:05:27,450 --> 01:05:30,090
The look in his eyes at your photo told the whole story.

1118
01:05:30,220 --> 01:05:32,420
Anyway, I sent Han Gyu Oh's contact info to your phone.

1119
01:05:32,490 --> 01:05:34,620
I refuse to give my daughter away...

1120
01:05:34,690 --> 01:05:36,960
to a family that tramples on people...

1121
01:05:37,130 --> 01:05:39,200
and acts so high and mighty like yours.

1122
01:05:39,400 --> 01:05:41,030
Please, just give up, Mu Jin.

1123
01:05:41,100 --> 01:05:44,200
No matter how hard I think, I can't remember.

1124
01:05:44,700 --> 01:05:46,300
Did you find what you lost?

